  **updateIterativeWeightedMean_**: `counter_tmp = 1 + (w*v)/cnt; denom_tmp = 1 + w/den; c *= counter_tmp/denom_tmp; then cnt += w*v; den += w`. The tool's `iwm` lambda (lines 756-759): `const double ct = 1.0 + (w * v) / cnt, dt = 1.0 + w / den; c *= (ct / dt); cnt += w * v; den += w;` — matches, assuming the cut-off lines are `cnt += w*v; den += w`. Yes, in actual OpenMS, updateIterativeWeightedMean_:

  ```cpp
  void MassTraceDetection::updateIterativeWeightedMean_(const double added_value, const double added_intensity, double& centroid_value, double& prev_counter, double& prev_denom) const
  {
    const double counter_tmp = 1 + (added_intensity * added_value) / prev_counter;
    const double denom_tmp = 1 + (added_intensity / prev_denom);
    const double weight = (counter_tmp / denom_tmp);
    centroid_value *= weight;
    prev_counter += added_intensity * added_value;
    prev_denom += added_intensity;
  }
  ```
  Yes, that matches my knowledge of OpenMS. Good — verify: yes, this is correct. So counters updated as stated.

  **updateWeightedSDEstimateRobust**: OpenMS:
  ```cpp
  double MassTraceDetection::updateWeightedSDEstimateRobust(const Peak1D& p, const double centroid_mz, double ftl_sd, double& last_weights_sum) const
  {
    double denom1 = std::log(last_weights_sum) + 2 * std::log(ftl_sd);
    double denom2 = std::log(p.getIntensity()) + 2 * std::log(std::abs(p.getMZ() - centroid_mz));
    double denom = std::sqrt(std::exp(denom1) + std::exp(denom2));
    double weights_sum = last_weights_sum + p.getIntensity();
    double tmp_sd = denom / std::sqrt(weights_sum);
    if (tmp_sd > std::numeric_limits<double>::epsilon())
    {
      ftl_sd = tmp_sd;
    }
    last_weights_sum = weights_sum;
    return ftl_sd;
  }
  ```
